Skipped Time is similar to Offline Time. There are only two ways to skip time: using a [[Market#Time|Time Warp]] from the Market; and casting {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Wormhole}} or {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Refined Wormhole}}. It is uncapped since v1.31.

<!-- if cheats are enabled, {NUM-9} or {F9} skips 1h of 'real' time -->

== Effects ==
Time Warps and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Wormhole}} stop all active spells, increasing casts as if completed normally. Casting {{SpellTooltip|Refined Wormhole}}, or {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Wormhole}} with {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Temporal Stabilizer}}, does not.

[[Void Entities|Void Mana]] is set to '''0'''.

Grants Mana, equal to:
<br><math>I \times O \times M \times T</math>

Grants [[:Category:Spells#Spell_Shards|Spell Shards]], equal to:
<br><math>S \times T</math>
<br>up to 1 day of skipped time (or enough to fill all scrolls on panel).

Increases Skipped Time by '''T'''. This affects Skipped and Played Game Time This Exile, Realm, and Total, as well as Character and Pet Game Time.

where:
*<math>I = \text{Idle Bonus} + 1</math>
*<math>O = \text{Offline Bonus} + 1</math>
*<math>M = \text{Mana per Sec}</math>
*<math>T = \text{Time Skipped, in Seconds}</math>
*<math>S = \text{Passive Spell Shard Generation}</math>

=== On Tick ===
Skipped time counts for the purposes of effects that activate on game tick, including:
* {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Synthetic Entity}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Nightfall}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Quasi-incantation}}, and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Refined Wormhole}} charging
* {{ClassTooltip|class_name=Ironsoul}} and {{ClassTooltip|class_name=Oni}} charging in Meditation stance
* [[Upgrademeister]] profit boost timer
* [[Balanced Darkness]] Liquid Shadow condition
This does not affect {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Chiropteric Rod}} charging; nor [[Trials]] of [[Trial_of_Innovation|Innovation]], [[Trial_of_Patience|Patience]], or [[Trial_of_Talent|Talent]].

=== Pets ===
Skipped Time counts as Offline time for the purposes of pets, granting XP and performing actions while offline:
* {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Spellhound}} grants Spell Shards.
* {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Daemon}}, {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Pit Lord}}. and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Living Sin}} grant Mana.
* {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Golem}}, and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Anima Construct}}, and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Nix-Instability}} gain XP.
* {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Doppelganger}} grants mana sources (except in [[Absorption]] challenge) and resets its XP pool to 10.
* {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Homunculus}}, {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Simulacrum}}, {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Soulstealer}}, {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Psychic Cacophony}}, and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Greater Chimaera}} grant mana sources and gain XP.
* {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Pixie}}, {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Zombie}}, {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Ent}}, {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Risen Giant}}, and {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Herald of Rot}} autoclick (up to 2,147,483,647 times) and gain XP.
* {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Mechanos Apexis}} casts {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Kelphior's Black Beam}} and gains XP.

=== Time Warps ===
Time Warps, unlike {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Wormhole}} and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Refined Wormhole}}, also count for Offline time towards:
* [[Pantheon|God XP]], including [[Praying]] XP gain
* [[Collectibles|Bat]] spawn rate boost and spawn timer
* [[Trials|Trial]] Rune Timer
* [[Attributes|Attribute]] Point Timer
* Trials of [[Trial_of_Innovation|Innovation]] and [[Trial_of_Patience|Patience]] completion


